hi it's matthew martin from details and  i just saw adam kimmel's collection and  i was loving the slimmer fit this season  it's a lot similar than it usually is  but you could tell that it still retain  the comfort and the masculinity that  he's really known for  the inspiration this season was cia and  air force special operations but i love  the fact that he took that idea and made  it more wearable and modern and updated  especially with a lot of the fabrics  the suits had all really trim peak  lapels which i really liked my favorite  suit in the collection was this  beautiful blue double breasted suit that  was a really elegantly tailored piece  for him but also looked really  comfortable  he paired a lot of the suiting and the  more tailored pieces with these work  boots and also a utility shoe it was a  great juxtaposition of a tailored item  with a more rugged shoe  was a great suede shearling bomber that  was really cool it was a really nice  update on a classic military piece  also i loved this hooded nylon jacket  that these patch pockets and around the  patch pockets he had all this beautiful  light blue top stitching which really  made the pocket stand out and took a  more classic utility piece and made it  look a lot more modern and chic  his collection is really versatile which  i love because you can really mix and  match all the pieces and easily  incorporate it into clothes you already  have follow me on twitter at detailsmat  and check out details.com for more  videos from paris
 

